SUMMARY:Rainy Day Bioacoustics: Listening to Birds with R - R-Ladies Vancouver
DESCRIPTION:As the Vancouver rain sets in, getting out into the field to listen to birds gets a bit trickier—but we can still tune in from the comfort of R! In this hands-on workshop, Sunny will introduce essential R packages designed for bioacousticians. We will walk through extracting bird sounds from Xeno-Canto, running machine learning models like BirdNET to detect species, and visualizing acoustic results—all within R! Along the way, we'll explore beautiful bird vocalizations and spotlight common Pacific Northwest species you hear around Vancouver, from the cheerful songs of Song Sparrows and Black-capped Chickadees to the ever-present Crows.\n\n\*\*\*\n\n1. If this is your first R-Ladies event, please take a moment to review our R-Ladies Global code of conduct: [https://github.com/rladies/starter-kit/wiki/Code-of-Conduct](https://github.com/rladies/starter-kit/wiki/Code-of-Conduct)\n2. Who is this allowed to attend the event?\n\nEveryone is welcome to join us at our events and to be a part of our mission to empower gender minorities with the skills and knowledge to code in one of the top programming language in data science, which is R.\n3\. To fulfill this mission we do ask participants to respect a focus on the encouragement and support for women and non\-binary people during our events\.
LOCATION:Vancouver Independent School for Science and Technology, 1490 W Broadway #200, Vancouver, BC V6H 1H5, Canada, Vancouver, CANADA
URL:https://www.meetup.com/rladies-vancouver/events/316720371/
ORGANIZER;CN=R-Ladies Vancouver:mailto:info@rladies.org
CATEGORIES:RLadies+,R-Ladies Vancouver
